{"id":"gen-68711ad11398afda","question":"I'm building an ML inference workflow where a model load is expensive but each prediction call is a quick, exception-safe computation. How should I combine sticky worker sessions with local activities to minimize both model-load and per-call latency, and which execution-mode settings will be ignored for the local prediction calls?","type":"cross_page","gold":[{"url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/building-workflows/activities/local_activities","anchor":null},{"url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/building-workflows/activities/sticky_worker_sessions","anchor":null}],"reference_answer":"Use a sticky worker session with sticky_to_worker=True for the load_model activity so the model loads once on a pinned worker, and run the quick predict calls inside run_activities_locally() to skip scheduling latency. However, sticky_to_worker (like rate_limit and heartbeat_timeout) does not apply to local activities, so pinning must come from the session around the model-load step.","language":"en","source":"generated","generator":{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","prompt_version":"v1","prompt_hashes":{"single_section":"4970bc4e4762400776a0a94005e312946ad382e07e23024894af4171fe0f6a22","cross_page":"085e21dfc9262fbbd8d51bb2a6b4acf264323de53d0504e955234b5703f98f67","capability":"e4432b33012475c8496c9187dc375fcf6b9626ccbb323af63444a802db5702da","api_reference":"fdfea635b8236dcbcc2c96235d099ef74b8ccd9ce12ac3e60c16e3c9f3fa9b90","post_cutoff":"ca45c4fe112ffadc4e7f00a16f1247d62622f36795369e27005b44b0f5ae9e28","unanswerable":"f7b884df810c1f1b6c10a61e1de84935840c20359d71567138fa47c275ff7644","filter":"cf348c523ad8613785ef3c104d685c01057bed02c1c6f8db16258a0f193fc5e8","page_alone":"86604a8deb155fe0d53d818fc18e9ff7679013375a087476b1ebb502713a7f1e","corpus_check":"4f76bb70e8f598174e0e20e336fdc90015b0e2ebd8c5a00cdc9a0109d93b4caf","closed_book":"c6763315257df0c22b7372deacc4bd59f9590582bf365a98b0875a240929498e"},"candidate_id":"cand-6b75b2686af5e139","seed_section":["https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/building-workflows/activities/local_activities","https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/building-workflows/activities/sticky_worker_sessions"],"run_dir":"eval/runs/2026-09-08-2218-dev-smoke","contributions":[{"url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/building-workflows/activities/local_activities","contribution":"Local activities run in the workflow worker process, so the sticky_to_worker parameter does not apply to them (rate limiting/worker pinning unsupported)."},{"url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/building-workflows/activities/sticky_worker_sessions","contribution":"Sticky worker sessions route activities to the same worker to reuse expensive in-memory resources like a loaded ML model, via run_sticky_worker_session and sticky_to_worker=True."}]}}
